WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.167
NumPy provides many mathematical functions that operate element by element.

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:10.742
These are often called universal functions.

00:00:10.742 --> 00:00:16.583
Examples include square root, logarithm, exponential, absolute value, minimum, and maximum.

00:00:17.045 --> 00:00:25.332
If we pass an array into one of these functions, NumPy applies the operation to every element and returns a new array.

00:00:25.332 --> 00:00:32.217
This is useful for transformations that appear in statistics and machine learning.

00:00:32.217 --> 00:00:39.827
For example, logarithms may be used to transform highly skewed data, while square roots and absolute values appear in

00:00:39.827 --> 00:00:48.211
many mathematical calculations. The important idea is that one function can process an entire numerical array at once.
